Features.Controls.SVG.Index
  SimpleStack
    Header 2|SVG Demo

    Header 3|HTML.SVG
    Text While most IntraWeb controls are higher level, there are HTML.* controls available for lower level access. This shows how to use a lower level control.
    Text HTML.SVG uses raw text to display SVG. It can be stored in IWML and visible in designer. It can be manipulated at runtime, but by changing the text data.
    Text Events are avaiable via traditional DOM methods.
    HTML.SVG
      Content:
        <rect x='10' y='10' width='80' height='80' fill='lightblue' stroke='black' />
        <circle cx='50' cy='50' r='30' fill='red' opacity='0.6' />
        <line x1='0' y1='0' x2='100' y2='100' stroke='black' />
        <text x='50' y='95' text-anchor='middle' font-size='10'>Test SVG</text>

    Header 3|SVG
    Text SVG Control which allow easier runtime manipulation and direct IntraWeb event support. SVG must be constructed at runtime.
